WEBVTT

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:03.630
Kaito! You and me still haven't settled the score yet!

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:04.940
Duel with me!

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:08.950
Interesting, in a manner of speaking this is the <i>real</i> final.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.260
All right, I accept, Yuma, Astral!

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.000
Yossha! <i>Kattobingu da ze</i>!

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:52.170
<i>Up to now, I have been fighting as a Numbers Hunter for Haruto's sake.</i>

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:54.500
<i>But...</i>

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:56.930
<i>But I...</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:04.340
Brother, are you going?

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:06.670
Sure.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.520
Brother...

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.260
It's fine, I definitly won't lose.

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:30.190
Brother...

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:46.450
Astral, somehow my whole body is tingly!

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:48.900
Mine too.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:50.970
That Kaito!

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:55.670
When we met him the first time, we almost would have lost.

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:02.400
And I turned into ZeXal with you, when we were fighting him inside the Emperor's Key.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:06.100
We also had a tag duel to save Haruto.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.950
That's why I think, that Kaito such a strong guy.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.210
But however I feel about that,

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:16.210
my aim is that I have to exceed him.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.220
Together with you, I will beat him for sure!

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:23.580
Yuma is bursting with his fighting spirit.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:27.630
I am somewhat exited as well <i>ura</i>!

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.820
Can Yuma-<i>kun</i> win against Kaito?

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:34.480
No clue, but this is the true final!

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.630
It's all right. As it's Yuma, he'll win for sure-<i>nya</i>!

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:42.580
What?

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.280
<i>Nya</i>-what's that sound?

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:45.960
That's...?

00:02:59.270 --> 00:02:59.970
Kaito!

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:04.510
I kept you waiting.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:12.490
Show me the mood you guys are in!

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:17.210
Kaito-<i>sama</i>, will you please teach that Yuma-dork a lesson!

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:18.660
Kaito...

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:23.650
Kaito, I'll finally settle this today.

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:25.450
I'll win!

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:30.080
With our duelist's pride on the stake, we will challenge you and win!

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:31.930
Yuma.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:33.510
Astral.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:35.840
With my full strength...

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:38.690
...I will fight you!

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:42.440
Let's get started!

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:45.420
Let's go!

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:47.660
Duel Disk: Set!

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.060
Duel Mode: Photon Change!

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:04.780
D-Gazer: Set!

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:14.100
<i>AR-Vision: Link established.</i>

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:17.270
Duel!

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:25.950
Brother...

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:33.250
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:38.800
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:55.500
<i>Hey, my friends, what scenery do you suppose</i>

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:01.200
<i>awaits us on the other side of this hill?</i>

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:05.810
<i>Hey, my friends, let's climb it together</i>

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:11.630
<i>It's too soon for us to turn back now</i>

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:17.030
<i>The time has come to combine
 together the power dwelling inside me</i>

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:22.310
<i>Gotta release my Soul Drive</i>

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:28.270
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:33.680
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:38.850
<i>Keep running, keep running, until you get there</i>

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:44.290
<i>Once again, once again, keep those challenges coming</i>

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:50.680
<i>My friends, keep on living in the here and now</i>

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:56.550
<i>Keep pressing onward together no matter what happens</i>

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.250
Go!

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:03.500
Yu-
Yuma!

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:06.550
You won't leave here until he has lost, clear?!

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:08.590
Sure, leave it to me.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:11.350
Numbers 72: The Time of Ultimate Showdown!

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:11.350
Yuma vs Kaito, The other Final of WDC!

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:12.180
Astral too, don't look so grumpy, you won't do your best!

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.140
Oh?! Don't tell me, you...

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:19.020
You can <i>see</i> this guy?!

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.480
Somehow, he has become visible for me.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:22.940
OH?

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.190
Apparently due to the effects in that battle,

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:29.950
my body seems to be something visible for some.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:33.740
Does that mean, that Shark, and Kaito too...?

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:38.000
What's up, Astral, Yuma? Don't you want to come at me?

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:41.250
Got it, let's go, I'm first!

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:43.290
My turn, draw!

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.920
I summon Ganbara Knight in attack position!

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:56.930
That guy... even though Ganbara Knight is switched into defense position, when he gets attacked...

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:02.810
In conclusion, usually summoning a Zero ATK monster in attack position is just...

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.780
Anyway, do your best, Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:06.900
Yuma.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:08.070
What's up.

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:09.400
It's good.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:14.990
I activate the permanent magic Zerozelock!

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:17.700
With the effect of this card,

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:22.540
Monsters on the field with Zero ATK can not be attacked!

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:29.420
With Kaito, it is very likely, that he brings out Galaxy-Eyes right at the beginning.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:34.010
Together with the effect of Ganbara Knight, this is a double solution to face the enemy.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.720
Yes. I end my turn with this.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:38.810
Now, will you come at me!

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:43.730
<i>Yuma, you sure have become stronger...</i>

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:47.110
But... My turn, draw!

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:52.700
When I have no monsters on my field, I can special summon this guy.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.240
Appear, Photon Slasher!

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:00.710
Then, I summon Photon Crusher, as usual!

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:09.130
Two monsters with 2000 or more attack.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:12.930
Knowing our defense, will he dare sticking to his plan to summon it?

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.720
I release my 2000 ATK Photon Crusher,

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:21.270
and my 2100 Photon Slasher!

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.060
Darkness within the shining galaxy...

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:27.310
Become the light of hope and live as my servant!

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:30.990
The incarnation of light descends!

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:35.780
Come forth! Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:44.000
Galaxy-Eyes.

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:46.130
Be buried in the Galaxy!

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:49.460
Galaxy-Eyes, attack Ganbara Knight!

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.550
Hold it, Kaito!

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:56.640
Due to the effect of Zerozelock you can't attack my Zero ATK Ganbara Knight!

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:01.140
I activate the quick play magic Galaxy Burst!

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:07.480
With this card, by halving the ATK of my Galaxy-Eyes,

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:12.530
I can negate the effects of up to 2 face-up cards on the opponents field!

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:20.410
The effect of Ganbara Knight and Zerozelock's effect are sealed!

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:26.670
My defense!

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:28.540
As to be expected from Kaito.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:35.130
He was ahead by a nose when summoning Galaxy-Eyes, in a manner of speaking.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.050
Galaxy-Eyes, attack Ganbara Knight!

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.600
Photon Stream of Destruction!

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:57.990
1500 damage all at once!

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:00.830
So he's still no match for Kaito-<i>ura</i>?

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.960
That's not the case!

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.540
That's right, Yuma, stand up!

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:11.290
I... I know... right.

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:17.720
Kaito! The duel has just begun!

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:20.180
Yuma...

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.140
<i>It's always like that.</i>

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:25.350
<i>How often will you stand up, again and again.</i>

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:27.180
Facing ahead...

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:32.230
I activate the permanent magic Battle Gravity!

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:39.200
With this card, when a player controls a monster, that did not battle,

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:42.240
he will receive 1000 points of damage.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:45.490
Wa... wait a sec! What do you mean?

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:51.460
So we have no other option that battling against Galaxy-Eyes.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:52.840
That is right.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:56.300
I set one card and end my turn!

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:00.800
The effect of Galaxy Burst ends.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.890
Galaxy-Eyes ATK and

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:06.310
the effect of Yuma's Zerozelock return to normal.

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:10.560
No matter how hard you try your strategy, it will fall flat on me.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:12.190
That's right, Kaito.

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:15.520
That's what I expect a duel with you to be like.

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.610
This happens and that happens and on it goes.

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:22.240
Isn't that totally fun?

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:24.200
Fun? Spas0?

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:27.290
You think, my tactics are fun?

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:29.540
I don't know anything about tactics.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:32.630
I am talking about the throbbing of the hearts.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.880
Throbbing of the heart?

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:38.050
Sure, that throbbing is in a duel too.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:39.970
That's what the <i>Kattobingu</i> is.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:45.600
And when I duel, I understand how amazing my opponent is.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:47.470
I have become a friend.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:51.060
You'll see,

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:55.110
the throbbing spreads and is given to everyone here.

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:56.270
Yuma...

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:57.570
In conclusion...

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:58.610
Yes-<i>ura</i>...

00:11:59.030 --> 00:11:59.530
<i>Cat...</i>

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:01.320
Heartbeat<i>bingu.</i>

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:02.910
He's like always.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:05.240
His mood is unbeatable.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:07.580
I've got the throbbing too,

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:10.040
from Yuma's and Kaito's duel.

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:17.380
Throbbing of the heart.

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:21.050
If you have this throbbing, everyone will become your friend!

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:22.970
You become one in a duel!

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:25.140
Kaito, don't you think that too!?

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:28.810
If that's the case, then show me your best!

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:29.850
Oh?

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:31.680
The Numbers!

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:36.230
My true victory will be defeating your Numbers.

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:38.770
Now, call the Numbers!

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:41.900
Sure, I'll show it to you.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:43.820
My <i>Kattobingu</i>!

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:46.660
My turn, draw!

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:49.990
I summon Goblindbergh!

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.960
When Goblindbergh is summoned successfully,

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:04.720
I can special summon a LV 4 or lower monster from my hand!

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.260
Come! Gagaga Magician!

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:16.270
I will overlay my LV 4 Goblindbergh and Gagaga Magician!

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:21.690
With these 2 monsters I built the overlay network!

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:23.940
Xyz-Summon!

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:31.040
Come forth, No. 39, Aspiring Emperor Hope!

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:37.420
It's there, Hope!

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:38.460
Good luck!

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:39.340
Yuma!

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:40.670
Hope.

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:44.970
Aspiring Emperor Hope attacks Galaxy-Eyes!

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:53.350
<i>Cat</i>! But why, when Hope has the lower ATK-<i>nya</i>?

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:59.730
I detach one overlay unit to negate Hope's attack!

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:04.610
I don't know what you're aiming at, but did you forget?

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:09.950
With the effect of Battle Gravity, because you don't battle, you get 1000 points of damage!

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:10.700
Yuma!

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:11.410
Sure!

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:17.000
I activate the quick spell Flash Effect!

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:20.170
When a Monster effect is activated during battle,

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:24.460
it increases this monster's ATK by 800,

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:28.680
and negates all effects of the monsters on the field!

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:30.260
What do you mean?

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:32.970
Then Galaxy-Eyes effect is...

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:34.770
It can't ban monsters anymore!

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:39.190
Hope's AKT increases to 3300!

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:46.610
Also, the monster effects of both, Galaxy-Eyes and Hope are negated!

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:49.570
Yuma, you...

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:54.030
Without the effect, Galaxy-Eyes can not ban Monsters,

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:58.080
and Hope's effect never negated the battle.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:02.000
This means, I increased the attack power and the battle continues!

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:05.460
Galaxy-Eyes' effect is held off too!

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:09.430
Go, Aspiring Emperor Hope!

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:13.220
Dream on!

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:15.760
Trap activate, Battle Simulation!

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:24.690
The battling monsters on both sides on the field have their ATK halved and will not be destroyed by battle!

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:28.940
Clever!

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:31.570
He did minimize the battle damage.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:33.320
Not a bad mood.

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:34.620
Kaito-<i>sama</i>!

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:36.370
I'm not done yet!

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:37.200
What!?

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:40.620
I activate the quick play spell Bi-Bind!

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:47.710
It can be activated, when the ATK of one monster on my field has dropped!

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:52.010
The attack power of that battling monster is doubled!

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:53.430
Say what!?

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:58.890
Plus the effect of Battle Simulation is negated and the opposing monster can be destroyed!

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:01.350
Impossible, Galaxy-Eyes will...

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:05.440
Go, Hope! Big Hope Sword Slash!

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:23.750
The effect of all traps and magic cards ends now,

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:26.590
and Hope's ATK and effect go back to normal.

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:32.170
I set one card and end my turn!

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:39.390
Got it!

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:42.230
I managed to inflict huge damage on Kaito!

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:51.280
<i>What'ya thinkin'? What'ya thinkin', Astral? Wasn't that awesome, right?</i>

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:52.900
<i>Am I not awesome? Really, really...?</i>

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.950
No matter how often he could have failed...

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:58.660
Or what pinch he was in...

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:02.500
He would never give up, desperately trying to stand up again.

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:06.920
Yes, and he enjoys dueling from the bottom of the heart.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:10.380
But as it is now, I...

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:17.340
Kaito...

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:23.140
Kaito, don't tell me...

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:23.810
Oh?

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:27.810
Yuma, Astral.

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:29.110
Kaito...

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:35.820
Brother... indeed...

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:41.660
This is...

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:43.450
...the end.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:44.500
Hu?

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:46.540
For me.

00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:48.630
I can't duel.

00:17:51.210 --> 00:17:53.340
I surrender the duel.

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:57.800
What are you talking about!

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:00.600
What's that with the 'I can't duel'?

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:04.850
Indeed Brother is...

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:06.770
What do you mean by that!

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:09.770
I...

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:13.280
... can't find any importance in dueling anymore.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:18.610
Kaito...

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:27.790
So far, I have been dueling only for Haruto's sake.

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:31.460
But, now that Haruto is saved,

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:34.250
all importance of fighting for me has disappeared.

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:38.010
Hence, by now I...

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:40.090
Kaito.

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:45.350
Give it a break! You have been my goal!

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:48.390
Quitting just like that, I'll never forgive you!

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:52.230
Yuma, I am unlike you,

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:54.820
I can't duel with passion anymore.

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:01.910
Kaito...

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:04.910
Kaito, there you are wrong.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:11.500
Yuma is fighting with me to collect the Numbers.

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:15.840
Victory will bring back my lost memories.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:19.170
But they are just a collection of the past.

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:24.260
Dueling with Yuma brought something much more important to me.

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:27.350
Something more important?

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:29.020
It's friends.

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:35.770
Through dueling, you are talking from heart to heart, deepening the bonds between friends.

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:38.400
Kaito, you are one as well.

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:41.820
For me, you are a very important friend.

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:44.280
Memories are things of the past.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:46.160
Friends represent the future.

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:50.540
You don't need to be tied to the past anymore.

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:55.920
And, besides, haven't you already noticed this?

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:59.170
Isn't it this why you have come here?

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:03.550
<i>Duelists really are close friends for each other!</i>

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:06.430
<i>And Dueling lets one change themselves and kattobingu on a whole new level!</i>

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:09.730
<i>Therefore, I will definitely take you to where Haruto is!</i>

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:12.890
I...

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:13.980
Kaito!

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:17.820
<i>Kaitobingu da,</i> Kaito!

00:20:26.030 --> 00:20:28.580
I can feel it, your throbbing!

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:29.580
Yuma.

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:33.870
But your throbbing shouldn't be just like that.

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:37.590
It should be more, much more! Show it to me!

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:40.210
Feel it, your <i>Kaitobingu</i>!

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:49.140
Kaito, this is all my fault.

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:54.480
With the expectations of us adults, I kept torturing Kaito.

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:57.310
Even now...

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:00.280
It's all right, father.

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:01.070
Oh?

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:04.910
Brother's eyes are trying to respond to Yuma.

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:11.910
That throbbing is getting a bit boring, right.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:15.330
Though don't know, what is lying ahead,

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:18.710
but I will open up my own path.

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:20.340
My own duel!

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:21.630
Kaito.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:22.760
Kaito.

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:28.510
It looks like Kaito has got his own dueling back.

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:32.970
Tsukumo Yuma, you really are a remarkable guy.

00:21:34.430 --> 00:21:35.850
Kazuma's son.

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:39.610
...alright, let's go! Back to our own home.

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:41.940
Chris,

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:43.610
Thomas,

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:45.530
Michael.

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:47.280
Yes, father.

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:54.580
Yuma, we will meet again.

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:00.840
Alright, come on, Kaito!

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:03.840
Here I come, my turn, draw!

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:15.980
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:22:15.930 --> 00:22:21.310
<i>Move on ahead, speeding up our throbbing beats</i>

00:22:26.950 --> 00:22:32.160
<i>Listen boys and girls, here's the secret to boys and girls like you</i>

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:36.200
<i>You're really just so spontaneous, wild as can be</i>

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:37.620
<i>I bet you didn't know?</i>

00:22:37.830 --> 00:22:40.290
<i>You might be a handful, but what's wrong with that?</i>

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:42.920
<i>Be up to no good, but learn for real</i>

00:22:43.040 --> 00:22:48.130
<i>Go the unpredictable route and shuffle your cards with a goal in mind</i>

00:22:48.300 --> 00:22:53.470
<i>Whenever you feel like you've lost your way, just take a minute to close your eyes...</i>

00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:59.100
<i>Shout "stop!" with all you've got, and there's your boundary line.</i>

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:05.570
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:23:05.860 --> 00:23:11.240
<i>We won't just stop here, not when we don't want to have any regrets.</i>

00:23:11.240 --> 00:23:16.330
<i>Even if we get hurt, we can't just hesitate now</i>

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:22.040
<i>We won't just give up, not when our future's a lot brighter than our today</i>

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:27.380
<i>Seriousness... It'll only make us keep fighting even harder</i>

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:32.840
<i>We'll always get as fascinated as we want, and we'll fight on every day</i>

00:23:41.100 --> 00:23:42.940
During the one-one-one duel with the rival Kaito,

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:47.400
both sides are using their full strength in those intensive exchanges.

00:23:47.940 --> 00:23:51.240
Just who will be blessed with the simile from Goddess of Victory?

00:23:51.660 --> 00:23:54.950
So this is the true Kaito, we will lose the moment we let our guard down!

00:23:55.120 --> 00:23:57.290
Yuma, let's come at him with all we've got!

00:23:57.700 --> 00:23:59.250
That guy is using the same method as I do!

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:01.410
Next, Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal:

00:24:01.580 --> 00:24:05.130
The Dream Grand Clash! Double Hope vs Double Galaxy-Eyes!

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:08.420
We will...<i>kattobingu</i> together!
